{
  "_comment": "Slot leases on a shared KV pool. On five fixed slots the lease scheduler removed re-prefill (follow-up cache hits 84%, re-prefill 0.2 s) without host RAM, but new tasks waited for a slot, because one or two of the slots were held over tool waits (vs the 5-slot + 4 GiB main line: P95 +21%, new-task TTFT P95 +325%). The same 24,576-token KV budget as the four-slot baseline, split into 8 slots with --kv-unified --kv-unified-per-slot 6144 (the pool was 37% used on average; task peak context median 2.7K), gives leases spare slots, so a hold no longer keeps new tasks out; no host cache is needed (the shared pool and the host cache together collapsed throughput). Leasing 6 or 8 of the 8 slots trades new-task waits against a larger decode batch. W1 0.95X, seeds 42-44; each seed's four runs go back to back with the main line and lease_p5 rerun alongside, because FIFO baselines drifted between sweeps. 12 runs, ~3 h. Before reading latencies check scheduler_summary in each lease run: pin_mismatches 0, followups_displaced near 0. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease_kvu --baseline fifo_c6_p5_cram4g; and lease_p5 as baseline with --baseline lease_p5.",
